["20260908142339","https://eba.europa.eu/regulation-and-policy/From%201%20January%202026,%20responsibility%20for%20all%20EU%E2%80%91level%20anti%E2%80%91money%20laundering%20and%20counter%E2%80%91terrorist%20financing%20%28AML/CFT%29%20tasks%20has%20moved%20from%20the%20European%20Banking%20Authority%20%28EBA%29%20to%20the%20new%20Anti%E2%80%91Money%20Laundering%20Authority%20%28AMLA%29.AMLA%20now%20develops%20and%20enforces%20the%20EU%E2%80%99s%20common%20AML/CFT%20rules,%20directly%20supervises%20selected%20high%E2%80%91risk%20financial%20institutions,%20and%20coordinates%20the%20work%20of%20national%20Financial%20Intelligence%20Units%20%28FIUs%29.For%20any%20AML/CFT%E2%80%91related%20information%20going%20forward,%20please%20visit:%20https://www.amla.europa.euAlthough%20the%20EBA%20no%20longer%20manages%20the%20AML/CFT%20rulebook,%20Article%2054%20of%20the%20AMLA%20Regulation%20ensures%20that%20all%20existing%20EBA%20AML/CFT%20guidelines%20and%20standards%20remain%20valid%20until%20AMLA%20replaces%20them.The%20EBA%20continues%20to%20contribute%20to%20safeguarding%20the%20EU%20financial%20system%20from%20money%E2%80%91laundering%20and%20terrorist%E2%80%91financing%20risks%20through%20its%20prudential%20supervisory%20work,%20including%20by:assessing%20ML/TF%20risks%20during%20authorisations%20and%20fit-and-proper%20assessments;overseeing%20ongoing%20supervision%20across%20the%20banking,%20payments,%20and%20crypto%E2%80%91asset%20sectors;promoting%20consistent%20supervisory%20approaches%20across%20the%20EU.For%20more%20details,%20consult%20the%20relevant%20legal%20acts%20within%20the%20Single%20Rulebook.","404","QE3FM24D2JNIRRAHS3J6AII6S2RMWAFI"]]
